\noindent
Let $G$ be a plane graph with outer cycle $C$, let $v_1,v_2\in V(C)$ and let $(L(v):v\in V(G))$ be 
a family of sets such that $|L(v_1)|=|L(v_2)|=2$, $|L(v)|\ge3$ for every $v\in V(C)\setminus\{v_1,v_2\}$
and  $|L(v)|\ge5$ for every $v\in V(G)\setminus V(C)$.
We prove a conjecture of Hutchinson that $G$ has a (proper) coloring $\phi$ such that
$\phi(v)\in L(v)$ for every $v\in V(G)$.
We will use this as a lemma in subsequent papers.
}

