The Track B profile is now explicit about the algorithmic fact: Thomassen-style proofs yield a quadratic constructive coloring algorithm, while the executable MRV proxy is exponential in general but follows a measured zero-backtrack \(O(N^2)\) scan on this distribution. This avoids presenting a fast empirical CSP run as a worst-case polynomial algorithm. I’m doing the final post-edit G1 and artifact consistency checks.
